# Build products — ~400 MB here, and fully reproducible from source.
build/
build-device/
DerivedData/
*.xcarchive

# Xcode per-user state. Never useful to anyone else, and a frequent source of
# spurious diffs.
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
*.xcscmblueprint
*.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/

# REAL EXPORTED HEALTH DATA — never commit.
#
# These are actual exports of the owner's Apple Health record: heart rate,
# workouts, activity summaries, and (when routes are enabled) GPS tracks that
# reveal home, work, and habitual routes and times. The README says to treat
# the export as sensitive; this is that rule enforced.
#
# Git history is effectively permanent, so an accidental commit here is not
# fixed by a later delete.
running_health_extract_*/
*.zip

# THE OWNER'S PERSONAL VALUES — this repository is public.
#
# Anything specific to the owner lives in these local files, each with a committed template:
#   Config/Local.xcconfig     Apple Developer Team ID       (template: Local.xcconfig.example)
#   scripts/local.env         phone and Watch device IDs    (template: local.env.example)
#   private/                  real run data, pre-public docs, the guard's pattern list
#                             (the install log is docs/INSTALLS.md, committed)
# scripts/check-sensitive.sh, run as a pre-commit and commit-msg hook, blocks any commit that
# would publish a value listed in private/sensitive-patterns.txt.
Config/Local.xcconfig
scripts/local.env
private/*
!private/README.md
!private/sensitive-patterns.example

# Local agent/editor settings — machine-specific, not project state.
.claude/settings.local.json

# macOS
.DS_Store
.gstack/
